1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
Meet Readmory.

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A quiet home for your books, your highlights, and the ideas you want to remember.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Import your reading data from Kobo, KOReader, or Kobalt.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Review what you are bringing in, then save it to your local library.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Browse your bookshelf, check your progress, and return to the books you have spent time with.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Search your highlights and notes to find a thought again, with the book it came from always close by.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Add your own reflections, and keep your personal notes together.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Let one good passage become the start of a new idea.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Explore your reading rhythm through a calendar of available activity.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
See the source behind each record, with estimates clearly marked.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Your library stays in your browser, with no account required.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Keep a backup, and try the Readmory public beta today.
